From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:45:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Initialise the shared authenticator of the first link once

Since commit 3cf7bf68f43d ("AP MLD: Fix deferred first link BSS's
authentication server init"), a link that is set up before the first
link of its AP MLD initialises the RADIUS client, the authentication
server and the IEEE 802.1X authenticator on behalf of the first BSS,
whose own setup waits for ACS, the HT40 scan or DFS. When the first BSS
is set up later, hostapd_bss_radius_init() skips the RADIUS client, but
authsrv_init() and ieee802_1x_init() run again. They give the first BSS
a second EAP server configuration and a second authenticator, and the
other links keep the first ones. One of the two pairs is never freed.

When the first link is then removed, the handover to the new first BSS
finds another authenticator there than in the removed BSS and moves
nothing. The authenticator of the remaining links keeps the removed BSS
as the context of its callbacks, and hostapd crashes on the next
association:

  WPA_TRACE: eloop SIGSEGV - START
  ap_get_sta_mld_links() ../src/ap/sta_info.c:107
  ieee802_1x_sta_entry_alive() ../src/ap/ieee802_1x.c:2490
  eapol_sm_sta_entry_alive() ../src/eapol_auth/eapol_auth_sm.c:902
  eapol_sm_step_run() ../src/eapol_auth/eapol_auth_sm.c:930

Skip both inits for a first BSS that already holds the objects, as the
RADIUS client init does. Set the WPS context of the EAP server
configuration then, since the init on behalf of the first BSS runs
before its WPS init. A failed init must not leave an object that the
skip then keeps: free what a failed RADIUS server setup leaves, and
free the authenticator when the driver setup, the RADIUS handler
registration or the WEP key setup fails.

A first BSS that is disabled before its own setup keeps its pointers to
the shared objects, because hostapd_free_hapd_data() returns early for
a BSS that was not started. Drop them when such a BSS leaves the AP MLD
and another link becomes the first BSS, so that a later init cannot
skip over objects that the new owner frees. Where such a BSS is the last
link, it keeps the objects of its earlier configuration over a disable
and enable, as it keeps the RADIUS client.

Fixes: 3cf7bf68f43d ("AP MLD: Fix deferred first link BSS's authentication server init")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/authsrv.c
+++ b/src/ap/authsrv.c
@@ -417,6 +417,14 @@ int authsrv_init(struct hostapd_data *ha
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
+	if (hapd->eap_cfg) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Skipping auth_serv init (already done)");
+
+		/* An init on behalf of this BSS ran before its WPS init */
+		hapd->eap_cfg->wps = hapd->wps;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 #ifdef EAP_TLS_FUNCS
 	if (hapd->conf->eap_server &&
 	    (hapd->conf->ca_cert || hapd->conf->server_cert ||
@@ -521,8 +529,10 @@ int authsrv_init(struct hostapd_data *ha
 
 #ifdef RADIUS_SERVER
 	if (hapd->conf->radius_server_clients &&
-	    hostapd_setup_radius_srv(hapd))
+	    hostapd_setup_radius_srv(hapd)) {
+		authsrv_deinit(hapd);
 		return -1;
+	}
 #endif /* RADIUS_SERVER */
 
 	return 0;
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1058,6 +1058,17 @@ void hostapd_bss_link_deinit(struct host
 		return;
 
 	hostapd_mld_remove_link(hapd);
+
+	/* Another link can set up the shared objects on behalf of a first BSS
+	 * that is not started, and hostapd_free_hapd_data() skips that BSS. */
+	if (!hapd->started && !hostapd_mld_is_first_bss(hapd)) {
+		ieee802_1x_deinit(hapd);
+		authsrv_deinit(hapd);
+#ifndef CONFIG_NO_RADIUS
+		hapd->radius = NULL;
+		hapd->radius_das = NULL;
+#endif /* CONFIG_NO_RADIUS */
+	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 }
 
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
@@ -2648,6 +2648,12 @@ int ieee802_1x_init(struct hostapd_data
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
+	if (hapd->eapol_auth) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "Skipping IEEE 802.1X state machine init (already done)");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	os_memset(&conf, 0, sizeof(conf));
 	conf.eap_cfg = hapd->eap_cfg;
 	conf.ctx = hapd;
@@ -2688,12 +2694,12 @@ int ieee802_1x_init(struct hostapd_data
 
 	if ((hapd->conf->ieee802_1x || hapd->conf->wpa) &&
 	    hostapd_set_drv_ieee8021x(hapd, hapd->conf->iface, 1))
-		return -1;
+		goto fail;
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_NO_RADIUS
 	if (radius_client_register(hapd->radius, RADIUS_AUTH,
 				   ieee802_1x_receive_auth, hapd))
-		return -1;
+		goto fail;
 #endif /* CONFIG_NO_RADIUS */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WEP
@@ -2708,11 +2714,15 @@ int ieee802_1x_init(struct hostapd_data
 		ieee802_1x_rekey(hapd, NULL);
 
 		if (!hapd->eapol_auth->default_wep_key)
-			return -1;
+			goto fail;
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_WEP */
 
 	return 0;
+
+fail:
+	ieee802_1x_deinit(hapd);
+	return -1;
 }
 
 
